lue":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T21:52:20-07:00","id":945286,"title":"","content":"The problem with Antediluvians and Arhats is they are both plot devices. They probably cannot survive a direct nuke (which is the equivalent power level of having a 1 TW solar power satellite focused on your head for 90 seconds), but they are pretty much invulnerable to anything less than that. A PC should not be within 100 miles of a fight between plot devices, not unless they want to be collateral damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T01:21:21-07:00","id":945355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magicballz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/938525-something-about-the-week-of-nightmares?p=938623#post938623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting. Arhats are considered to be as powerful as Antediluvians right? What good is that power if they can't use it.</div> </div> </div> </div>What you're essentially asking is &quot;which Deus Ex Machina has a bigger McGuffin Power?&quot; The answer, as always, is the Deus Ex Machina with the cooler McGuffin Power, as dictated by you and your Storyteller.<br /> <br /> Or one of the Saulots. There's at least five of him at my last count.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T15:16:21-07:00","id":945701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/938525-something-about-the-week-of-nightmares?p=945286#post945286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with Antediluvians and Arhats is they are both plot devices. They probably cannot survive a direct nuke (which is the equivalent power level of having a 1 TW solar power satellite focused on your head for 90 seconds), but they are pretty much invulnerable to anything less than that. A PC should not be within 100 miles of a fight between plot devices, not unless they want to be collateral damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why I dramatically tone them down. An Antedeluvian is a vampire and just a vampire. It's an absurdly powerful one but the PCs could theoretically kill one through various crazy means they use to kill Methuselah up to and including Dominating the US military to drone striking their Temple or all of them diablierizing it at once while wearing protection against mind-control.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T10:56:48-07:00","id":958805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magicballz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/938525-something-about-the-week-of-nightmares#post938525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So there were three Bodhisattva that fought against the Antediluvian. Where were the Arhats? How come they did join in on the fight?</div> </div> </div> </div>You must understand that Arhat have ascended to an higher state of spiritual being, by all means is like if they are in golconda.<br /> This makes them more detached from the mundane world, pretty much like the old salubri methuselah of old or the inconnu.<br /> <br /> But remember that the bodhisattva that fought Ravanna where not common bodhi, Eight Thuder Sage was a virtual Arhat, Black Earth Boy was the most favoured disciple of the Arhat Resplendent Crane and undisputd master among kue-jin of the disicipline of yang prana e jade shintai, same goes for the Crane.<br /> <br /> We are talking of bodhi as powerful as the most powerful western methuselah, at the time they were the best the kue-jin could throw at Ravanna.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T01:32:03-07:00","id":959147,"title":"","content":"Besides there is a common misconception:it is tought that Arhat are as powerful as Antedeluvian or much more powerful than a bodhisattva.<br /> <br /> This is not the case, Arhats are respected as Antediluvians but it is clearly stated that they are more or less on the same power level ofa bodhi ora methuselah.<br /> <br /> The true difference doesn't pertain power but spiritual enlightment, to use a western paragon an Arhat is to a Bodhisattva what a methuselah in Golconda is to a common methuselah.<br /> <br /> In fact being a bodhisattva or an arhat is more a matter of choiche than else, the bodhis are on the verge of mastering their dah, but they choosed to postpone trascendence in order to help other kue-jin progress,just because becoming an Arhat (just as entering Golconda) implies the detachement from the mundane world.<br /> <br /> In fact when KotE explains the various level of Darmha's mastering Bodhisattva and Arhat are treated in the same section, since an arhat is a special kind of bodhi.<br /> <br /> In this section it is both said that arhat have the social standing of an Ante<br /> <br /> &quot;In many ways, the arhats hold a social standing and respect akin to what kindred accord to antedeluvian&quot;<br /> <br /> And that being an arhat means living like an hermit &quot;tough unlike those terriblr Cainites kue-jin arahts keep completely to themselves and do not interfere in the affairs of the greater Kue-jin society&quot;<br /> <br /> This is on page 35<br /> <br /> <br /> Their power level is instead explained on page 11<br /> <br /> &quot;The mightiest scions of the Dharmas- the bodhisattvas and the arhats - are as potent as any kindred methuselah and much more enlightened&quot;<br /> <br /> Furthermore at the Dharma table is shown that at Dharma 10 you can be either a Bodhisattva or an Arhat, so the most powerful bodhi can be as powerful as Arhat.<br /> The difference between a dharma 10 bodhi and a dharma 10 arhat lies in their social status and in their personal enlightenment, not in their sheer power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 08-28-2016, 07:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T12:22:37-07:00","id":959368,"title":"","content":"This thread just reminds me of why I hate Week of Nightmares so much. The Antediluvians are supposed to be godlike beings that transcend lesser creatures like humans and other vampires - it was prophesied that they would usher in a Biblical style end of the world. Once you drop a nuclear (spirit) bomb on and use space satellites to burn it to death, you're not playing V:tM anymore, you're playing Rifts and all you need to kill the Antediluvian is enough megadamage. <br /> <br /> In fact, any kind of crossover where you introduce godlike beings from other lines is going to undermine the themes and mythology (reality?) of VtM and so I think it was a wise choice to keep Arhats and other powerful being out of Gehenna.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T13:23:48-07:00","id":959406,"title":"","content":"Well it's not like it went down easily.<br /> <br /> He devoured all the 4th and 5th gen members of his clan, crushed kue-jin temples under his feet, killed all the vampire in Kolkata, sent wave of nightmares all over the world, wreaking havoc in evey psychiatric ward of the globe, he couldn't be toppled by three of theost powerful vampire of the east, survived an horde of demons and wraiths and resisted not one but four spirit nukes, and just after this he succumbed to the force of four suns,and if this is not enough he destroyed his whole clan.<br /> <br /> Even more with his death he opened the door for the werewolves' apocalypse and for the greatest cataclysm the umbra has ever seen, the avatar storm.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> (besides I'm totally convinced that Ravana didn't died, it was all a ruse with chimestry 10 to convice the others that he was a threat no more and to get his hands on a lot of souls destroyed by the radiations)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T13:30:09-07:00","id":959411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/938525-something-about-the-week-of-nightmares?p=959406#post959406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even more with his death he opened the door for the werewolves' apocalypse and for the greatest cataclysm the umbra has ever seen, the avatar storm.</div> </div> </div> </div>How so? A few packs (maybe Septs) went down, but on a worldwide scale it didn't really do anything. The Avatar Storm was a plot point for Mages. It literally made no difference to Werewolf (I don't even remember it being mentioned).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T14:06:14-07:00","id":959449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/938525-something-about-the-week-of-nightmares?p=959411#post959411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How so? A few packs (maybe Septs) went down, but on a worldwide scale it didn't really do anything. The Avatar Storm was a plot point for Mages. It literally made no difference to Werewolf (I don't even remember it being mentioned).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Apocalypse<br /> <br /> Page 37, scenario: The last battleground.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;So the triatic wyrms, full of anger and rage, brooded in Malfeas and planned their revenge. To prevent their simple eviction from the penumbra, they required an anchor to fix them within it. In fact they needed three: one for the Eater of Souls, one for the beast of war and one for the Defiler. These anchor would take the form of ritual sacrifices of monster whose lives and deaths both utterly embodied the aspect of the Triatic Wyrm they would tie tight to this world. These sacrifices would be known as the Scions of the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> The first of these Sacrifices was made in 1997 in Bangladesh, India.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> And so on.<br /> <br /> Ravana was chosen as the avatar of the Eater of souls upon earth.<br /> With his ritual death the Eater of souls managed to get out of Malfeas and enter the Aetherial Realm starting the road to the Apocalypse.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ( what where we saying about the common lore?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 08-28-2016, 05:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T14:10:40-07:00","id":959454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/938525-something-about-the-week-of-nightmares?p=959449#post959449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Apocalypse<br /> <br /> Page 37, scenario: The last battleground.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those books aren't canon. Not really. They are a collection of ideas for how to run an endgame scenario. In that one scenario, you are retconning what happened with [Ravnos] to be significant to the Werewolf line as a whole. Outside of 1/4 of possible Apocalypse scenarios, the Ante dying didn't matter and didn't have any greater effect.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T16:13:15-07:00","id":959549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magicballz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/938525-something-about-the-week-of-nightmares#post938525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So there were three Bodhisattva that fought against the Antediluvian. Where were the Arhats? How come they did join in on the fight?</div> </div> </div> </div>A Kuei-jin becoming Arhats is virtually (if not physically) ascended to the Heaven, so it's more akin to a spirit (maybe not Celestine-tier, but certainly an Incarna), so they will probably act more like a powerful spirit would (see for examples Werewolf TA), while emboding their Dharma (i.e. a Crane Arhat probably will never incite meaningless chaos, even at the cost of losing the opportunity to strike).<br /> <br /> Furthermore, I did remember a Bodhisattva on some book that ascended to Ahrat right after the Week of Nightmares.<br /> My thought was &quot;the coward ran away&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https: